{
  "slug": "project-version-workflow",
  "name": "Project Version Workflow",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Manage project's versions and iterations by a standard workflow on Claude Code. Generates a daily version tag (e.g. v260416), records the changes in update_log.txt along with the git username when available, commits them, and optionally pushes to remote. It checks for a clean repo, asks you to confirm the change summary, warns about sensitive files, and never force-pushes.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `update-commit` (Generate a dated version tag, create a professional conventional-commit, tag it, and optionally push), `update-commit-bypass` (Non-interactive version of update-commit), `view-update-log` (Use when the user wants to see git commit history, version changelog, update log, or project history)\n- **Commands** (1): `update-commit-plugin`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install project-version-workflow@claude-community` from `ATreep/project-version-workflow`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
